From f37e44960a5f8252aa4d7c641a50fbf621974a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:01:43 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Ad hoc: sceNetAdhocMatching over the ad hoc server

A matching engine (host/adhoc/matching.*) for sceNetAdhocMatching's parent,
child and P2P modes: hello messages with the game's own data, requests,
accepts, cancels, byes, keepalives and data with acknowledgement, between
the group's members over the ad hoc server. Its events (HELLO, REQUEST,
ACCEPT, ESTABLISHED, LEAVE, BYE, DATA, DATA_ACK, TIMEOUT...) reach the
game's handler as interrupts from the vblank. The accepting side reports
ESTABLISHED as soon as it accepts; a game that leaves the group right after
ACCEPT does not wait for a confirmation round.

Also:
- sceNetAdhocctlGetPeerInfo.
- sceNetAdhocPtpOpen refuses a second socket on the same local port to the
  same peer, so a game that reopens its stream every frame until the
  connection takes holds one.
- sceNetAdhocPtpSend and PtpRecv write 0 to the length on would-block,
  timeout or error: a game that adds the length to its count either way had
  stalled a 3,744-byte message.

Checked with Dissidia 012: two copies on one computer and this PC against a
Steam Deck (LAN and the internet) go from its Online Lobby through the
challenge and fighter select into a battle, and back for a rematch. Not
checked: another game, Group Battle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
